[common]
displayName="Frigate"
desc="Frigate is an open-source NVR for home surveillance, designed for Home Assistant, with AI object detection. It uses OpenCV and TensorFlow to run real-time object detection on IP camera streams locally.<br>Note! On first launch the admin password is printed in the Docker log. Right after installation, open the Docker app and <strong>look for the password in the Frigate container logs</strong>."

[entry]
title="Frigate"

[install]
welcomeStepTitle="Welcome to Frigate"
greetingText="Thanks for using Frigate."
introText="Frigate is a complete local network video recorder (NVR) designed for Home Assistant, with AI object detection. It uses OpenCV and TensorFlow to run real-time object detection on IP cameras locally.<br>The project is still in pre-release and is not yet a 1.0 product, so please refer to our <a href='https://docs.frigate-cn.video/'>documentation</a> when using it.<br><br>Follow us:<br><a href='https://space.bilibili.com/3546894915602564' target='_blank'>bilibili</a><br><a href='https://qm.qq.com/q/uikrC4l46A' target='_blank'>QQ group</a><br><br><h2>Before installing:</h2>This is an AI based NVR with real hardware requirements. Very old hardware is not supported (Intel <strong>6th generation or newer</strong>, J-series CPUs are only partially supported). Even a newer low-end machine is a better choice than a very old platform, so please keep this in mind. See <a href='https://docs.frigate-cn.video/frigate/planning_setup' target='_blank'>the documentation</a> for details."
versionStepTitle="Select the installation variant"
versionLabel="Variant"
versionRequiredMessage="Select the variant to use"
versionDefaultLabel="Default"
versionTensorrtLabel="NVIDIA GPU"
versionRocmLabel="AMD GPU"
versionRkLabel="Rockchip"
versionHelpText="Frigate supports several hardware acceleration options.<br>Use the default image for Intel integrated or discrete GPUs. It also supports Coral and Hailo8 accelerators.<br>If you have an NVIDIA GPU, choose <strong>NVIDIA GPU</strong>.<br>For an AMD integrated or discrete GPU, choose <strong>AMD GPU</strong>.<br>For Rockchip SoCs, choose <strong>Rockchip</strong>.<br><br>Note that NVIDIA also requires <strong>NVIDIA Container Toolkit</strong> to be installed from the app store first.<br>AMD hardware acceleration is not supported on older integrated GPUs."
coralStepTitle="Hardware acceleration"
coralLabel="Use a Coral accelerator?"
coralNoneLabel="None"
coralUsbLabel="USB Coral"
coralM2Label="M.2 Coral (driver must be installed manually)"
coralHelpText="Coral is an edge AI accelerator available in USB and M.2 versions. The M.2 version is the best value but requires an extra driver.<br>Note: in most cases this accelerator is not needed, since even an Intel integrated GPU handles video decoding and AI detection very well."
featureStepTitle="Feature settings"
hfMirrorLabel="Enable Huggingface model download mirror"
hfMirrorYesLabel="Yes"
hfMirrorNoLabel="No"
githubMirrorLabel="Enable Github model download mirror"
githubMirrorYesLabel="Yes"
githubMirrorNoLabel="No"
mirrorHelpText="Downloads of the built-in models are accelerated by mirrors provided by the <strong>Frigate Chinese documentation site</strong> and <a href='https://cnb.cool' target='_blank'>cnb.cool</a>"
shmSizeLabel="Shared memory size (shm)"
shmSizeRequiredMessage="Enter the shared memory size with a unit, for example mb"
shmSizePatternMessage="Invalid format, use a value such as 512mb or 1gb"
shmSizeHelpText="Frigate uses shared memory (shm) to process video frames. If this value is too small, using several high-definition cameras will cause 'Bus error'. See <a href='https://docs.frigate-cn.video/frigate/installation#calculating-required-shm-size' target='_blank'>the documentation</a> for details."
networkStepTitle="Network and authentication"
networkModeLabel="Network mode"
networkModeRequiredMessage="Select the network mode"
networkBridgeLabel="Bridge mode (default)"
networkHostLabel="Host mode"
networkHelpText="<strong>Bridge mode</strong>: the container uses the Docker bridge network and exposes services through port mappings.<br><strong>Host mode</strong>: the container shares the host network directly. Performance is better but all container ports are exposed on the host.<br>If you use Xiaomi cameras or Apple HomeKit, choose <strong>Host mode</strong>, otherwise the cameras may not be discovered."
authLabel="Authentication"
authRequiredMessage="Select the authentication mode"
authGatewayLabel="fnOS unified gateway (recommended)"
authNativeLabel="Frigate built-in authentication"
authHelpText="<strong>fnOS unified gateway</strong>: sign in with your fnOS account, no extra password to remember.<br><strong>Frigate built-in authentication</strong>: access the HTTPS port directly with a separate Frigate username and password. Configure port forwarding yourself if you need external access."
finalStepTitle="Final important reminder"
warningHelpText="<h1>Warning!</h1><br>Note that if you chose Frigate built-in authentication, the password is printed in the Docker log on first launch. Right after installation, open the Docker app and look for the password in the Frigate container logs.<br>See <a href='https://docs.frigate-cn.video/configuration/authentication#resetting-admin-password' target='_blank'>the documentation</a> for other ways to recover the password."
agreeLabel="I understand this"
agreeRequiredMessage="Please read the warning above, otherwise the app cannot be used properly"

